# KNOWN GAP todo/t1087 — `Deque[T].get(i)` loses the element type when `T` is
# an aggregate, and binds the payload as `int`.
#
# `gg check` is clean and the program runs to rc 0, printing a small integer
# instead of the string. Adding `.len()` to the bound value fails at link with
# `undefined reference to 'int64_t__len'`, which is what names the binding.
#
# One axis varied, three ways: `Vector[String].get(0)` is correct, and
# `Deque[int].get(0)` is correct — only the aggregate element on a Deque is
# wrong. No higher-order call appears anywhere in the program.
#
# Intended: prints `aabc`, rc 0, on both backends.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Deque[String] v = Deque[String]()
    v.push(mk("aa", "bc"))
    if v.get(0) is Some(x):
        print(x)
    else:
        print("none")
